{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings of length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. This is classic. We can use recurrence: Let a_n be number of length n strings ending with run of length 1 of some bit? Actually we need states: last run length and bit. Let's define DP[n][b][k] where b=0/1, k=1 or 2 (run length). For n=1: DP[1][0][1]=1, DP[1][1][1]=1. For n>1: transition: if next bit same as b, then k+1 must be <=2. If next bit different, new run length 1. So recurrence: DP[n+1][b][1] += sum over other bit b' of DP[n][b'][1]+DP[n][b'][2]. DP[n+1][b][2] += DP[n][b][1] (since only from run length1 same bit). Can't go to length3. Compute up to n=12. Let's compute quickly.\n\nInitialize n=1:\nDP1: b0,k1=1; b1,k1=1.\n\nn=2:\nCompute DP2[b][1] = sum over other bit of DP1[other][1]+DP1[other][2] (none with k2). So DP2[0][1] = DP1[1][1]+DP1[1][2]=1+0=1. Similarly DP2[1][1]=1.\nDP2[b][2] = DP1[b][1] =1 each. So DP2: (0,1)=1,(0,2)=1,(1,1)=1,(1,2)=1. Total 4.\n\nn=3:\nDP3[0][1] = sum over other bit: DP2[1][1]+DP2[1][2] =1+1=2.\nDP3[1][1] = DP2[0][1]+DP2[0][2] =1+1=2.\nDP3[0][2] = DP2[0][1] =1.\nDP3[1][2] = DP2[1][1] =1.\nTotal =2+2+1+1=6.\n\nn=4:\nDP4[0][1] = DP3[1][1]+DP3[1][2] =2+1=3.\nDP4[1][1] = DP3[0][1]+DP3[0][2] =2+1=3.\nDP4[0][2] = DP3[0][1] =2.\nDP4[1][2] = DP3[1][1] =2.\nTotal=3+3+2+2=10.\n\nn=5:\nDP5[0][1] = DP4[1][1]+DP4[1][2] =3+2=5.\nDP5[1][1] = DP4[0][1]+DP4[0][2] =3+2=5.\nDP5[0][2] = DP4[0][1] =3.\nDP5[1][2] = DP4[1][1] =3.\nTotal=5+5+3+3=16.\n\nn=6:\nDP6[0][1] = DP5[1][1]+DP5[1][2] =5+3=8.\nDP6[1][1] = DP5[0][1"}}],"created":1790936963,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt